	(text "Relay 1 (safety light): drive PA8, INA236 U2 at 0x40"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 111.76 22.86 0)
		(effects (font (size 2 2) (bold yes)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "30ee00f5-ef90-53ef-b202-2a936bab7b85")
	)
	(text "No coil feedback: PA0-PA3 drive the winch and the servo UART; the INA236 does the diagnosis.\nINA236 0x40 (A0 = GND): load current (30 mΩ, LSB 100 µA) + 24 V rail (read on IN-); ALERT → PA15.\nLED4: output ON; its 6.7 mA also lets the INA236 see the contact close with no load.\nF3: 3A hold PTC, so a shorted output trips only this channel. D12: load flyback.\nQ2 AO3400A: R9 100 Ω gate, R10 100k pull-down = OFF in reset (CIF §7a)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 269.24 91.44 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "3dbb2718-4d52-57cd-a0a7-a6a1f0a2347e")
	)
	(text "Relay 2 (LED DRL): drive PC6, INA236 U3 at 0x41"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 111.76 127 0)
		(effects (font (size 2 2) (bold yes)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "7efd9d4f-f2fb-5a6b-84c4-1b3aa7079062")
	)
	(text "No coil feedback: PA0-PA3 drive the winch and the servo UART; the INA236 does the diagnosis.\nINA236 0x41 (A0 = VS): load current (30 mΩ, LSB 100 µA) + 24 V rail (read on IN-); ALERT → PA15.\nLED5: output ON; its 6.7 mA also lets the INA236 see the contact close with no load.\nF4: 3A hold PTC, so a shorted output trips only this channel. D13: load flyback.\nQ3 AO3400A: R12 100 Ω gate, R13 100k pull-down = OFF in reset (CIF §7a)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 269.24 195.58 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "f44a2838-c27e-52fd-a087-b26e06434938")
	)
	(rectangle
		(start 15.24 20.32)
		(end 106.68 250.19)
		(stroke (width 0) (type dash))
		(fill (type none))
		(uuid "b20a028a-6d2f-540e-92ba-239a98ebadd7")
	)
	(text "Relay diagnosis (CIF §7b, INA236 only)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 17.78 22.86 0)
		(effects (font (size 2 2) (bold yes)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "a3620fc4-cf5d-5662-930a-e87d35543fac")
	)
	(text "Coil supply = +5V_24 (U1 DC/DC, Power sheet).\nRead ≥ 30 ms after switching.\n\nOFF, I ≈ 0 → OK, relay off\nOFF, I > 3 mA → contacts welded or driver\n   shorted\nON, I in window → OK (LED 6.7 mA + load)\nON, I ≈ 0 → relay not closing: open coil,\n   driver or GPIO, no +5V_24, contact,\n   output PTC or input fuse open, or no 24 V\nON, I over limit → short / stall (ALERT → PA15)\nany, VBUS < 20 V → 24 V supply fault\n\nNo coil feedback on this board (differs from\nCIF §2c / §7a): PA0 / PA1 drive the winch and\nPA2 / PA3 are the servo UART (USART2). So an\nopen coil or a dead driver looks the same as a\ncontact that does not close: \"ON, I ≈ 0\".\nI = INA236 load current, VBUS = 24 V rail.\n\nINA236 (30 mΩ; CIF §6a names the INA226, swapped\nfor its 50 V rating, review M1): CONFIG 0x4327,\nCAL 1707 (LSB 100 µA, FS 2.73 A),\nMASK/ENABLE 0x8001 (SOL, latched),\nALERT limit 30000 = 2.5 A default; set each\nchannel's value from the CANopen dictionary.\n\"Current present\" threshold 3 mA (the LED alone\ndraws 5.1-6.7 mA over 21-29 V).\nOn ALERT LOW: read MASK/ENABLE of each INA236\n(AFF bit 4) to find the channel; the read also\nclears the latch. Switch it OFF, report on CAN.\nUnlike the INA226: bus LSB 1.6 mV, bus read on\nIN- (no VBUS pin), Device ID 0xA080."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 17.78 27.94 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "216aceef-63bd-543f-9e23-68ae0f30ada2")
	)
